# Every text file checks out with LF, on every machine and whatever core.autocrlf says (M43 U9).
# This repository's text is read byte for byte: tests take fixtures and `.format.md` files apart
# by `\n`, and the builds embed migrations and pack notes as raw strings, so a Windows checkout
# with git's default autocrlf=true failed tests and would have shipped other bytes. Nothing here
# needs CRLF, and git still decides what is binary (text=auto).
* text=auto eol=lf

# A .emd is text or SQLite bytes, chosen per file (D-246). Neither may have its line
# endings rewritten: the text is byte-identical by design (D-245) and the reader already
# normalizes CRLF, and SQLite bytes are not text at all. -text leaves both untouched;
# git still shows the text form as a readable diff because it contains no NUL bytes.
*.emd -text
